//! 🧬️ En1993 artifact — snapshot mutation dispatch. Semantic vocabulary derived from
//! `📸️snapshot/🦀️.rs`'s `En1993Snapshot` shape (a flat EN 1993 design-check input sheet —
//! 74 persistent scalar fields, no id-keyed/index-keyed collections, no hierarchy) per
//! `.🧬semio/🦑️repo/🎫️tickets/🎆️26/🌙️08/☀️12/SEMANTIC-MUTATIONS-OVERHAUL/📓️taxonomy.md`/
//! `📓️derivation-rules.md`. `impl protocol::Mutation`/`SemanticMutation` below are generated by
//! `#[derive(dsl::Mutations)]` — never hand-written.
//!
//! Every field maps to exactly one of 17 mutations: `change-annex` for the lone document-identity
//! scalar (the national annex choice), plus 16 `update-<family>-inputs` mutations, one per EN 1993
//! part (`⚙️engine/🦀️.rs`'s `check_full_steel_member` groups the very same fields the same
//! way — one `#[region]` per part, each calling exactly one check function with exactly that part's
//! fields). Per `📓️derivation-rules.md` rule 1, `change-<field>` is the default for document-root
//! scalars and `update` is reserved for a field group that's genuinely "validated together, never
//! meaningfully set one-field-at-a-time" — that bar is met here because every group's fields are
//! consumed as a single unit by exactly one EN 1993 check function (e.g. `bolt_e1_mm` alone means
//! nothing without `bolt_e2_mm`/`bolt_d0_mm`/... — together they ARE "the bolted connection"), unlike
//! e.g. `shooting`'s scene facet where the app sets each field independently. The 11-field
//! `update-member-properties` group is the base steel member's own forces/section/material state,
//! consumed by `part_1_1`'s five checks plus reused by `part_2`/`part_3`/`part_5`/`part_6` — the
//! taxonomy's own "analysis settings" example. `silo_t_mm`/`silo_r_mm` are shared by both the
//! `part_1_6` shell-buckling check and the `part_4` silo-wall check (same physical silo), so both
//! live in one `update-silo-shell-inputs` group rather than being split or duplicated.
//!
//! Every triad leaf is mounted directly as a `mutations`-sibling module in `🦀️.rs` (this lane's
//! agent owns `🦀️.rs`, so no self-wiring `#[path = "."]` blocks are needed here — the orphaned
//! `🟤️set-snapshot` stub is deleted along with its dangling glue mount).

